from pathlib import Path
import shutil
w=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
p=w.parent/'outputs/MarioSouls controls and notes.txt'
s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8').replace('local build 0.2','local build 0.3')
s=s.replace('Start: return to native controls and open the Dark Souls menu.','Y (top face button): interact with the nearby object. The normal game prompt still shows A.\nStart: open the Dark Souls menu while Mario stays visible.')
s=s.replace("Mario's movement, A/B and LT are withheld", "Mario's movement, A/B/Y and LT are withheld")
s=s.replace('Switch back with F6 or the stick-click shortcut for ladders, doors, bonfires, dialogue, items, and menus. Use the normal Dark Souls controls, then press F6 when standing safely on solid ground. Q is your normal interaction key; End opens the game menu.', '''INTERACTIONS WHILE STAYING MARIO
Stand close to the object and face it, then tap Y on the controller or Q on the keyboard. Allow about a second for the handoff. Dark Souls handles the interaction while Mario stays visible with an adapted door, climbing, or sitting animation.
On ladders: use the left stick up/down, or W/S. You can pause halfway. Mario movement resumes automatically after dismounting onto solid ground.
At bonfires: use the normal menu controls (A to select, B to close; Enter on keyboard). Mario movement resumes after leaving the menu and standing up.
Start or End opens the normal game menu without hiding Mario. Close it to return automatically.
If no interaction starts, Mario returns to normal movement after a short pause. Move closer and face the object before retrying. Without a connected controller, Q may need a second tap after the handoff has settled.
F6 or the stick-click shortcut still manually switches between Mario and the normal character. Avoid manually toggling while attached to a ladder.

Verified in the Asylum: resting/leaving the courtyard bonfire and jumping afterward; climbing the first ladder up and down, pausing on a rung, and automatically resuming; opening the courtyard shortcut gate and walking through it; opening/closing the regular game menu. These are adapted SM64 animations, so Mario's hands and feet do not exactly match every rung, handle, or native animation.''')
s=s.replace('Moving platforms, elevators, dynamic doors and breakable objects are not fully integrated with Mario physics. Use native controls for these interactions.', 'Moving platforms, elevators, dynamic doors and breakable objects are not fully integrated with Mario physics. The new interaction handoff handles tested doors and ladders, but does not add their geometry to Mario collision. Elevators and other untested interactions may still need manual native mode.')
s=s.replace('Mario mode turns off on death, a character/map change, or a detected large native teleport.', 'Mario mode, including interaction display, turns off on death, a character/map change, or a detected large native teleport.')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
